# {{title}} — GPU Compute Shader for aetherion-continuum

## Purpose
Compress sparse field data (SparseNode arrays, field tensors, gradient buffers) on GPU using learned basis projection inspired by Headroom's Kompress-base model.

## Architecture

```
Input Field/Sparse Data → ContentType Detection → Basis Projection → Residual Quantization → CompressedBlock
                                                              ↓
                                                    CCR Store (for reversibility)
```

## Shader: `gpu_kompress.wgsl`

### Bindings (group 0)
| Binding | Resource | Purpose |
|---------|----------|---------|
| 0 | `input_data: array<f32>` (read) | Source field/sparse elements |
| 1 | `basis_vectors: array<f32>` (read) | Pre-trained basis (loaded from host) |
| 2 | `compress_params: CompressParams` (uniform) | Config: block_size, basis_dim, quant_bits |
| 3 | `compressed_blocks: array<CompressedBlock>` (read_write) | Output compressed blocks |
| 4 | `compress_stats: CompressStats` (read_write) | Atomic counters for ratio/error |

### Key Constants
```wgsl
const BASIS_DIM: u32 = 64u;           // Latent dimension
const BLOCK_SIZE: u32 = 256u;         // Elements per compression block  
const QUANT_BITS: u32 = 8u;           // Residual quantization (256 levels)
const MAX_RESIDUAL: f32 = 1.0;        // Clipping threshold
const COHERENCE_THRESH: f32 = 0.01;   // Skip if already coherent
```

### Entry Points
| Function | Workgroup | Purpose |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| `gpu_kompress_compress` | 64 threads | Compress field/sparse blocks |
| `gpu_kompress_decompress` | 64 threads | Reconstruct from CompressedBlock |
| `gpu_kompress_collect_stats` | 1 thread | Compute avg compression ratio |

### Data Structures

```wgsl
struct CompressParams {
    total_elements: u32,
    block_size: u32,
    basis_dim: u32,
    quant_bits: u32,
    max_residual: f32,
    coherence_thresh: f32,
    content_type: u32,  // 0=field, 1=sparse, 2=gradient, 3=hash
}

struct CompressedBlock {
    basis_indices: array<u16, 4>,    // Top-4 basis vector indices
    residual_quant: array<u8, 256>,  // Quantized residual per element
    residual_scale: f32,             // Dequantization scale
    coherence: f32,                  // Input coherence (0-1)
    original_norm: f32,              // L2 norm of original block
}

struct BasisVector {
    weights: array<f32, 256>,        // Basis vector (BLOCK_SIZE)
}
```

### Pipeline Integration

Add to `ZeroSyncDispatch`:

```rust
// In ShaderModules
pub gpu_kompress: wgpu::ShaderModule,

// In run()
let gpu_kompress_src = include_str!("../../core/gpu_kompress.wgsl");
gpu_kompress: device.create_shader_module(...),

// Create pipeline
let kompress_bgl = device.create_bind_group_layout(...);
let kompress_pipeline = device.create_compute_pipeline(&ComputePipelineDescriptor {
    label: Some("gpu_kompress"),
    layout: Some(&kompress_pipeline_layout),
    module: &shader_modules.gpu_kompress,
    entry_point: "gpu_kompress_compress",
});

// Dispatch in frame (after field_tensor, before conservation)
{
    let mut cpass = encoder.begin_compute_pass(...);
    cpass.set_pipeline(&self.kompress_pipeline);
    cpass.set_bind_group(0, &self.kompress_bind_group, &[]);
    cpass.dispatch_workgroups(num_blocks, 1, 1);
}
```

### ContentType Routing

| ContentType | Detection | Basis Source | Use Case |
|-------------|-----------|--------------|----------|
| 0 (field) | `field.x != 0` | Global PCA on field tensors | Dense field compression |
| 1 (sparse) | `nodes[].active == 1` | SparseNode PCA (morton + depth) | Sparse octree compression |
| 2 (gradient) | `length(grad.xyz) > 0` | Gradient PCA | Gradient field compression |
| 3 (hash) | `hash_table[].next != 0` | Spatial hash patterns | Hash table compression |

### Reversibility (CCR-style)

- Original stored implicitly: `basis_indices + residual_quant + residual_scale`
- Exact reconstruction: `dequantize(residual) + sum(basis[basis_indices])`
- Quality metric: `reconstruction_error = ||original - reconstructed|| / ||original||`
- Target: <1% error for field, <0.1% for sparse nodes

### Performance Targets

| Metric | Target | Measurement |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| Compression ratio | 4-8x | `original_bytes / compressed_bytes` |
| Reconstruction error | <1% | L2 relative error |
| Latency | <1ms/block | GPU timestamp queries |
| Throughput | >10M elements/s | `total_elements / frame_time` |

### Host-Side Basis Training

```python
# Offline: compute PCA basis from field snapshots
from sklearn.decomposition import PCA
import numpy as np

snapshots = load_field_snapshots()  # (N, 256)
pca = PCA(n_components=64).fit(snapshots)
basis = pca.components_.astype(np.float32)  # (64, 256)
save_to_gpu_buffer(basis)
```

